write('PROJECT_INVENTORY.md', `# Project inventory\n\n${common}\n## Actual architecture\n\nLinawLetra is a Filipino reading application with Admin, Teacher, Parent and Student roles. React 19, TypeScript 6, Vite 8, React Router 7, TanStack Query, Tailwind 4, Recharts and Supabase JS implement the frontend. Express 4/CommonJS on Node implements the API; Supabase provides Auth, PostgreSQL, RLS, Storage and Realtime. Nodemailer handles server SMTP; ElevenLabs supplies TTS; browser speech APIs supply recognition. PDF upload/extraction uses Multer, pdf-parse and pdf2json. Forms use component state and validation; package presence alone does not establish use of every installed library.\n\nFrontend routing: src/App.tsx and src/routes/*Area.tsx. Backend: server/server.js mounts /api/admin, /teacher, /parent, /student, /notifications, /auth, /tts and the explicitly anonymous /public/tts alias. Browser code also accesses Supabase directly, making database RLS a separate security boundary. Bearer authentication and current-role/status authorization run on the server. Hosted frontend configuration is public/.htaccess; backend deployment is server/railway.json; CI builds/tests and can deploy on main pushes. No deployment was invoked.\n\n## Exhaustive source indexes\n\n${table(['Index','Count','Artifact'], [['Files (source/configuration/assets/tests/scripts)',''+inv.files.length,ref('inventory.json')], ['Functions including inline callbacks/test helpers',''+inv.functions.length,ref('FUNCTION_INVENTORY.csv')], ['Product functions excluding tests/maintenance scripts',''+productFunctions.length,'subset of function index'], ['API declarations',''+api.length,ref('API_AND_ROUTE_INVENTORY.csv')], ['UI Route declarations, including layouts/fallbacks',''+uiRoutes.length,ref('API_AND_ROUTE_INVENTORY.csv')], ['Interactive source templates',''+controls.length,ref('CONTROL_INVENTORY.csv')], ['Data-access expressions',''+inv.dataAccess.length,ref('DATABASE_DEPENDENCIES.csv')], ['Web migrations',''+inv.migrations.length,ref('inventory.json')], ['Historical documentation/evidence files',''+inv.documentationArtifacts.length,'inventory.json documentationArtifacts']])}\nFunction rows record name, file/line, source-derived purpose/expected operations, actual verification limit, dependencies, conditions, error handlers, testing status and test references. This is a complete AST index of declarations, not a claim of individual human review or runtime coverage of every function/branch. A test mentioning a name is only a candidate reference. Inline callbacks and shared controls cannot be assumed passed from a parent screen pass.\n\n## Every page\n\n${table(['Page','Area','Static importers','Full signed-in workflow status'], pages.map(p => [ref('../'+p.file,p.file),p.area,p.importedBy.join(', ')||'None found: review legacy/unrouted status',/pages\/(admin|teacher|parent|student)\//.test(p.file)?'BLOCKED':'NOT RUN at whole-page scope; see executed public subcases']))}\n## Every API and UI route\n\n${table(['ID','Kind','Method/path','Location','Whole-workflow status'], inv.routes.map(r=>[r.id,r.kind,(r.method||'')+' '+r.path,ref('../'+r.file,r.file+':'+r.line),r.status]))}\nPOST /api/public/tts reuses the TTS factory with anonymous middleware and an IP limiter; it is an additional mount rather than another declaration. GET /api/health is local and covered by real HTTP assertions.\n\n## Database and configuration\n\n${table(['Migration','Created tables','Contains data-changing SQL','Full replay'],inv.migrations.map(r=>[r.file,r.tables.join(', ')||'alter/function/policy/data migration',r.mutatesData,r.status]))}\nMigrations start with web-specific additions; they do not establish a complete empty-project baseline. No file was executed against shared Supabase. A minimal disposable local fixture is separately blocked by host setup; historical reports are not fresh results. Environment variable names only are indexed in inventory.json; private env values were never copied into reports. Dependencies are pinned in root/server lockfiles. The optional scripts/qa-tools workspace is tooling, not the deployed application.\n\n${table(['File','Documented variables'],['.env.example','server/.env.example'].map(f=>[f,inv.configuration.filter(r=>r.file===f).map(r=>r.name).join(', ')]))}\n## All source/configuration files\n\n${table(['File','Kind','Area','Recorded status'],inv.files.map(r=>[r.file,r.kind,r.area,r.status]))}`);
write('FUNCTIONALITY_AUDIT.md', `# Functionality audit\n\n${common}\n## Execution and classification rules\n\nThe module workflows below are BLOCKED at the full authenticated/persistent scope. Their local unit, middleware and mocked-route subcases have independent results. All source-defined controls and functions have explicit statuses in the CSV indexes; NOT RUN means no independently attributed functional test, even when a containing module has passing tests. Unrouted/legacy files remain in the inventory and are not treated as exposed features.\n\n${caseTable(workflows)}\n## Actual local outcomes\n\n${table(['Suite','Results','Evidence'],[['Backend mixed unit/integration suite',backend.counts,ref('evidence/final/backend.tap')],['Frontend units',frontend.counts,ref('evidence/final/frontend.tap')],...browser.map(b=>[`${b.name} ${b.version}`,count(b.rows),ref(`evidence/browser-recheck/local-${b.name}.json`)]),['Word-of-day failure-recovery probe',count(probes),ref('evidence/transaction-probes.json')]])}\nSee FUNCTIONAL_TEST_CASES.md for every executed assertion and every API/control requirement. Public browser passes verify anonymous screens at resized desktop widths. They do not exercise signed-in dashboard CRUD. Browser request policies deny non-GET/HEAD and external networking. Selected frontend units substitute Auth/Supabase/React boundaries; these are not DOM/browser integration tests.\n\n## Dormant and incomplete functionality\n\nAdmin settings persist preferences; persisted session timeout, failed-login, maintenance, reward and curriculum preferences are not proof that every setting changes runtime behavior. Source search does not establish global enforcement. Existing teacher scheduling/bulk selection placeholders and an advancement-badge placeholder predicate are retained in historical QA; they must not be treated as complete implemented workflows. The formerly inert Admin header search now filters and navigates existing pages; it does not search personal records. Real microphone recognition, TTS audio quality, email delivery, MFA, Storage and Realtime remain BLOCKED.\n\n## Every page classified\n\n${table(['File','Whole feature status','Reason'],pages.map(p=>[p.file,/pages\/(admin|teacher|parent|student)\//.test(p.file)?'BLOCKED':'NOT RUN',p.importedBy.length?'See routed workflow and narrower executed cases':'No static/dynamic importer found; do not assume this legacy page is routed']))}`);
write('UNIT_TEST_READINESS.md', `# Unit test readiness\n\n${common}\nThe built-in Node test runner is the existing framework; no test dependency was added. Pure speech scoring, Filipino phonemes/syllables, curriculum progression, reading insights, validation, PDF validation, calendar/streak rules, credential reporting, authorization and saved-profile units are independently testable. Mocked router tests additionally exercise actual Express routing with synthetic persistence and Auth boundaries. React helper tests transpile components into an isolated VM with explicit hook/router/API substitutions; they do not certify DOM focus or browser rendering.\n\n## Executed suites\n\n${table(['Suite','Counts','Evidence'],[['Backend (contains unit and integration tests)',backend.counts,ref('evidence/final/backend.tap')],['Frontend isolated units',frontend.counts,ref('evidence/final/frontend.tap')],['Coverage-instrumented backend',coverageCounts,ref('evidence/backend-coverage-final.tap')]])}\nNew tests cover all discovered wrong-role API combinations and declared UUID parameters, active/inactive shared endpoints, complete-notification marking, settings toggle types and persistence failure status, example-configuration hygiene, and Admin search filtering/navigation/empty/Escape behavior. Existing tests retain normal, invalid, empty and boundary cases.\n\n## Actual code coverage\n\n${coverage ? `Node/V8 reports **${coverage[0]}% lines, ${coverage[1]}% branches, ${coverage[2]}% functions** for loaded matching backend JavaScript files, excluding server/tests and node_modules. This is tool-produced execution coverage, not whole-repository coverage. Unloaded modules/maintenance scripts and frontend TypeScript are outside this denominator. The detailed per-file uncovered lines are in the raw coverage report.` : 'Coverage report could not be parsed; no percentage claimed.'}\nThe initial broad include accidentally included server/node_modules; its report is retained as backend-coverage.tap but is not used for first-party coverage claims. Corrected exclusions are recorded in the rerun command.\n\n## Every discovered function\n\n[FUNCTION_INVENTORY.csv](FUNCTION_INVENTORY.csv) contains ${inv.functions.length} definitions, including ${productFunctions.length} product definitions. Per-function runtime status is conservative NOT RUN unless independently attributable; file coverage and name references do not prove all branches or requirements. Focus further units on student mutation failure recovery, promotion ordering, enrollment compensation, PDF draft replacement rollback, provider cancellation/timeouts, persisted preference enforcement and isolated React state/empty/error behavior.\n\n## Executed Node assertions\n\n${caseTable([...backend.rows,...frontend.rows])}`);
write('INTEGRATION_TEST_READINESS.md', `# Integration test readiness\n\n${common}\n## Verified local boundaries\n\nReal local HTTP tests instantiate the production Express app using a loopback-discard Supabase URL and synthetic key. They cover health, security/CORS/version/request headers, malformed/oversized JSON, unknown paths and anonymous rejection for every discovered protected endpoint. They never execute successful database CRUD. Other integration tests run actual routers with mocked persistence/Auth/Storage boundaries, including cross-parent material ownership, drill input/history protection, Admin settings and atomic-assignment RPC error mapping. Nodemailer stream composition and Multer multipart upload are exercised locally without SMTP. TTS tests mock synthesis, dictionaries, fallback and rate limits.\n\nThe expanded ${ref('../server/tests/auditRoleMatrix.test.js')} invokes actual Express routers in process, with real role middleware and a fake profile store. All 235 combinations pass. Its first HTTP transport run had 71 fetch failures; that evidence is retained as role-matrix-http-original.tap. The transport was changed explicitly to avoid the environment's loopback dependency. An in-process pass does not clear the HTTP transport failures.\n\n## Database boundary\n\nThe disposable PostgreSQL runner never loads application env files and uses random synthetic local credentials. The first run failed during initdb restricted-token setup. An approved outside-sandbox retry failed with listen EACCES on 127.0.0.1. Both evidence files and verifier FAIL outcomes remain recorded; the planned SQL assertions were not executed in this audit. They are BLOCKED, not regression passes inferred from older reports.\n\n## Every full API integration\n\n${caseTable(apiCases)}\n## Required isolated environment\n\nOwner confirms there is one shared Supabase project and no staging. A separate project needs an authoritative schema-only baseline, migrations reviewed against that baseline, synthetic curriculum/relations, Admin/Teacher/Parent/Student plus unrelated-owner accounts, real non-service-role JWTs for RLS tests, private Storage fixtures and mail/TTS sandbox configuration. Do not replay migrations or provisioning scripts against the current shared project. The guarded .qa/staging.env workflow remains disabled. Full Auth/PostgREST/Storage/RLS/Realtime/SMTP/provider integration, rollback durability and concurrent requests remain BLOCKED.\n\nThe Word-of-Day failure probe is an executed mocked integration failure (AUD-005), separate from database execution. Atomic SQL remediation needs schema review and isolated validation; no speculative shared migration was applied.`);
write('FUNCTIONAL_TEST_CASES.md', `# Functional test cases\n\n${common}\nEach row includes ID, module, objective/feature, preconditions, steps, expected/actual results, status, evidence and defect. Rows represent different scopes and overlap: do not sum them into independent requirements or code coverage. API-FLOW and FLOW rows deliberately remain BLOCKED even if negative middleware subcases pass. CTRL rows index JSX templates rather than the number of rendered DOM instances.\n\n${caseTable(functional)}`);
